# Chronicle Harvest

## Core Instruction
Treat Chronicle as a high-coverage but fallible evidence stream: detect useful changes, preserve evidence and confidence, write candidate signals to the harvester outbox, and leave promotion to the Chief of Staff.

## Required Inputs
- Chronicle skill and its preconditions
- Chronicle summaries under `$HOME/.codex/memories_extensions/chronicle/resources/`
- Chronicle OCR/frame data under `$TMPDIR/chronicle/screen_recording/` only when summaries need targeted confirmation
- Machine state at `{{WORKSPACE_PATH}}/vault/Operations/.machine/chronicle-harvest/state.json`
- Candidate outbox at `{{WORKSPACE_PATH}}/vault/Operations/.machine/chronicle-harvest/outbox.jsonl`
- CoS doctrine at `[[vault/Operations/Chief of Staff System.md]]`
- Signal lifecycle rules at `{{WORKSPACE_PATH}}/vault/Operations/SIGNAL_INBOX.md`

## Default Workflow
1. Read this skill and the Chronicle skill before touching Chronicle data.
2. Verify Chronicle is currently running and screen-history data is fresh enough to use.
3. Read `state.json` to determine the last successful reviewed timestamp and last reported timestamp.
4. Select the smallest useful window:
   - default to new Chronicle summaries since `last_successful_run_at`
   - if no prior run exists, review the most recent 3-6 hours
   - if the gap is too large, summarize the broad gap and sample recent/high-signal periods instead of exhaustively reading everything
5. Use summaries first. Use OCR grep and sampled frames only to confirm important or ambiguous observations.
6. Classify each candidate as one of:
   - `active_work`
   - `idle_project_signal`
   - `durable_fact`
   - `possible_action`
   - `possible_decision`
   - `needs_verification`
   - `noise`
7. For each candidate, assign:
   - `confidence`: `high`, `medium`, or `low`
   - `proposed_destination`: `ignore`, `cos_review`, `action_ledger`, `decision_queue`, `domain_note`, `project_note`, or `source_verification`
   - evidence pointers: Chronicle summary filenames, OCR timestamps, frame paths, or a note that evidence is summary-only
8. Append only new, non-duplicate candidate JSON objects to `outbox.jsonl`.
   New candidates start with `status: "new"`. CoS later owns review and may
   change status to `promoted`, `dismissed`, `superseded`,
   `needs_verification`, or `ignored_noise`.
9. Update `state.json` with the run timestamps, reviewed window, counts, and any blocker.
10. Report to CoS only when there are high-signal new candidates, a blocker, or a repeated failure mode. Otherwise stay quiet.

## Candidate JSON Shape
Each `outbox.jsonl` line must be a single JSON object:

```json
{
  "id": "chr_YYYYMMDDHHMM_short_slug",
  "created_at": "iso-8601-with-offset",
  "observed_window_start_utc": "iso-8601Z",
  "observed_window_end_utc": "iso-8601Z",
  "category": "active_work|idle_project_signal|durable_fact|possible_action|possible_decision|needs_verification|noise",
  "confidence": "high|medium|low",
  "summary": "short factual candidate",
  "evidence": ["summary filename, OCR timestamp, or frame path"],
  "proposed_destination": "ignore|cos_review|action_ledger|decision_queue|domain_note|project_note|source_verification",
  "verification_needed": true,
  "status": "new",
  "notes": "short reason this matters or why it was rejected"
}
```

After CoS reviews a candidate, the same line may gain lifecycle review fields:
`reviewed_at`, `reviewed_by`, `decision`, `destination`, `reason`, and
`superseded_by`. Harvester runs should preserve those fields and avoid
near-duplicate candidates unless there is materially new evidence.

## Rules
- Do not treat Chronicle as ground truth for completed actions, purchases, submissions, account changes, or sent messages; mark those `needs_verification` unless another authoritative source has already confirmed them.
- Do not write directly to `ACTION_LEDGER`, `DECISION_QUEUE`, `Notes and Journal`, or domain/project notes from this skill.
- Do not resurrect a candidate CoS already reviewed unless there is materially new evidence; read reviewed statuses and `superseded_by` before appending near-duplicates.
- Do not create broad life summaries or diary entries.
- Do not infer intent from visible content alone; describe what was visible and why it may matter.
- Do not promote sidebar visibility, open tabs, or casual browsing into active work without corroborating evidence.
- Do not include sensitive personal details unless they materially change an operational task, decision, or durable context item.
- Do not duplicate an existing unresolved outbox candidate; update state counts instead.
- Do not use OCR text as an authoritative source for IDs, links, or exact text when a connector, file, or app API can verify it.
- Do not notify {{USER_NAME}} directly unless the Chronicle system itself is blocked or a high-risk time-sensitive signal appears and CoS is unavailable.

## Exception Rule
If Chronicle is unavailable, stale, or too noisy to review safely, update `state.json` with `last_error`, append no candidates, and report the blocker to CoS only if it prevents scheduled harvesting for more than one run.

## Output Contract
- Update `state.json` on every attempted run.
- Append candidate JSON lines to `outbox.jsonl` only for new candidates.
- In the harvester thread, summarize only:
  - reviewed window
  - candidate counts by category
  - high-signal items for CoS
  - blockers or repeated flaws
- Stay silent when no useful candidate or blocker exists.
